// vk_const — the Vulkan constants the backend uses.
//
// Written from the Khronos registry (`vk.xml`) for the commands and records the
// backend uses, each size and offset measured by a C compiler against
// `<vulkan/vulkan.h>`. The script that first produced it is not part of this
// tree: the file is maintained by hand, and `vk_layout_check` is what holds the
// records to C — at start-up, before the first one reaches a driver, and in
// `examples/gpu_check`.

// Every value is an `i32` (VK_WHOLE_SIZE an `i64`): Axle refuses an unsigned
// top-level `const`, and a 32-bit field lays out the same signed or not.

// ---- results, formats, usage and state flags

